nfty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{x{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f338d77ee01746b9a0b348615cc7f4946f6911bf5686ee5f3f9adbf5eeafa1c3" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d1