/13972402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-x-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{e}^{x}-x-1]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-x-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1} & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{e}^{x}-1]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/state.json" "file_sha256" "bef90c10f3fe2496b1b1e7b74213c83c0789cb68a20aa5b4aef87a1bb7dab9b6" "basis" 669 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "603662a2371e1969ab72279b0b36b42f98ae7df8ff393373cd979c98c7ad1b95" "basis" 669 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-fiel